      "question": {
        ":question/id": "566b3719-5491-54ac-b3d8-02352bfb3991",
        ":question/problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, $\\log_{256}(4)$ equals{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X=\\frac{\\log_b X}{\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=256$ and $X=4.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{256}(4) &=\\frac{\\log_{2}(4)}{\\log_{2}(256)} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\log_{2}({2}^{2})}{\\log_{2}({2}^{8})} \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{8} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
